==English==
[[Image:Clenched human fist.png|thumb|right|A clenched [[fist]].]]

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|ang|en}} {{m|ang|beclenċan}}, [[causative]] of {{m|ang|clingan||cling}}. Compare {{m|en|stink}} and {{m|en|stench}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{rhymes|ɛntʃ|lang=en}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|es}}

# [[tight|Tight]] [[grip]].
# {{lb|en|engineering}} A seal that is applied to formed thin-wall [[bushing]]s.
# A [[local]] [[chapter]] of the {{w|Church of the SubGenius}} [[parody]] [[religion]].
#* {{quote-text|year=1989|author=Ted Schultz|title=The Fringes of Reason|page=210|passage=And perhaps most innovative of all, Drummond and Stang pushed for a policy of '''clench''' autonomy {{...}}}}
#* {{quote-text|year=2003|author=Peter Knight|title=Conspiracy Theories in American History: An Encyclopedia|page=170|passage=Every SubGenius '''clench''' is required to have a member who does not believe {{...}}}}
#* {{quote-text|year=2012|author=George D. Chryssides|title=Historical Dictionary of New Religious Movements|page=95|passage=Originality is encouraged, and some '''clenches''' have devised their own distinctive organizational names {{...}}}}

